/* =====================================================================
   BUCKETLIST.JS — the world's 100 most iconic travel landmarks &
   wonders, for the Bucket List picker on choose.html.

   Ranked most-iconic first, by cross-referencing five major published
   lists: New7Wonders of the World, the UNESCO World Heritage List,
   Lonely Planet's Ultimate Travel List, TripAdvisor Travelers' Choice,
   and National Geographic's iconic-places lists. 'sources' names the
   lists each place appears on; 'city' links a landmark to the nearest
   featured city page when there is one (~2 h away or less).

   img  = a local file under images/bucketlist/ (downloaded from each
          landmark's Wikipedia/Wikimedia Commons photo, July 2026) —
          no more live fetch, so photos always load correctly.
   page = the Wikimedia Commons file page (photo credit link), shown
          under every photo as "Photo: Wikimedia Commons".
   Compiled July 2026; ranks 85-100 re-verified July 2026; all 100
   photos downloaded to local files July 2026 (3 filenames corrected
   during download: #67 Sheikh Zayed Grand Mosque, #87 Maya Bay,
   #93 Kinkaku-ji — originals had been renamed/removed on Commons).
   ===================================================================== */

